#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2.2 Color the coupling map {#22-color-the-coupling-map}"
msgstr "2.2 Obarvení mapy vazeb {#22-color-the-coupling-map}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let us study how we color the coupling map of a backend.  This is needed to "
"group $ZZ$ interactions into layers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Podívejme se, jak se obarvuje mapa vazeb (coupling map) backendu. To je "
"potřeba k seskupení $ZZ$ interakcí do vrstev.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To begin with, let us visualize the coupling map of a backend.  Note the "
"coupling maps are heavy-hexagonal for all the current IBM Quantum devices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nejprve si vizualizujme mapu vazeb backendu. Všimni si, že u všech "
"současných zařízení IBM Quantum jsou mapy vazeb typu heavy-hex.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/utility-i/extracted-"
"outputs/84e11b8e-bc74-4f3a-8538-d4d34d069e0f-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/utility-i/extracted-"
"outputs/84e11b8e-bc74-4f3a-8538-d4d34d069e0f-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To color a coupling map, we use [rustworkx](https://www.rustworkx.org/), "
"which is a Python package for working with graphs and complex networks.  It "
"provides multiple coloring algorithms, which are all heuristic and thus "
"aren't guaranteed to find a minimal coloring.\n"
msgstr ""
"K obarvení mapy vazeb použijeme [rustworkx](https://www.rustworkx.org/), což"
" je Python balíček pro práci s grafy a komplexními sítěmi. Poskytuje několik"
" obarvovacích algoritmů, které jsou všechny heuristické, a proto není "
"zaručeno, že najdou minimální obarvení.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Having said this, since heavy-hex graphs are bipartite, we pick up "
"[graph_bipartite_edge_color](https://www.rustworkx.org/apiref/rustworkx.graph_bipartite_edge_color.html),"
" which should find a minimal coloring for these graphs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nicméně vzhledem k tomu, že grafy heavy-hex jsou bipartitní, zvolíme "
"[graph_bipartite_edge_color](https://www.rustworkx.org/apiref/rustworkx.graph_bipartite_edge_color.html),"
" který by pro tyto grafy měl najít minimální obarvení.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Heavy-hexagonal graphs should be painted in three colors.  Let us check this"
" for the above coupling map.\n"
msgstr ""
"Grafy typu heavy-hex by měly být obarveny třemi barvami. Ověřme si to pro "
"výše uvedenou mapu vazeb.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Yes, it is!\n"
msgstr "Ano, je to tak!\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For fun, let us paint the coupling map to the coloring obtained, using the "
"feature of rustworks visualization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pro zábavu si namalujme mapu vazeb získaným obarvením, s využitím "
"vizualizační funkce rustworks.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/utility-i/extracted-"
"outputs/fb9b6915-5ace-4104-b81d-91666e689f0d-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/utility-i/extracted-"
"outputs/fb9b6915-5ace-4104-b81d-91666e689f0d-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"3. Solve the Trotterized time evolution of a 2D Ising model. {#3-solve-the-"
"trotterized-time-evolution-of-a-2d-ising-model}"
msgstr ""
"3. Vyřešení Trotterizované časové evoluce 2D Isingova modelu. {#3-solve-the-"
"trotterized-time-evolution-of-a-2d-ising-model}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let us define a routine to construct a circuit of the utility paper for the "
"time evolution of a 2D Ising model.  The routine takes three parameters, a "
"backend, an integer indicating the number of Trotter steps, and a Boolean "
"controlling the barrier insertion.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pojďme definovat rutinu pro sestavení obvodu z článku o užitečnosti pro "
"časovou evoluci 2D Isingova modelu. Rutina přijímá tři parametry: backend, "
"celé číslo udávající počet Trotterových kroků a booleovskou hodnotu řídící "
"vkládání bariér.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Please note that we have already manually performed qubit mapping and "
"routing for the circuit constructed.  Thus, when we transpile the circuit "
"later, we do not (__should not__) ask the transpiler to do qubit mapping and"
" routing. As you will soon see, we invoke it with the optimization level as "
"1 and the layout method as \"trivial\".\n"
msgstr ""
"Všimni si, že jsme pro sestavený obvod již ručně provedli mapování a routing"
" qubitů. Proto, když obvod později transpilujeme, nepožadujeme (__neměli "
"bychom požadovat__) po transpileru, aby prováděl mapování a routing qubitů. "
"Jak za chvíli uvidíš, voláme ho s úrovní optimalizace 1 a metodou layoutu "
"„trivial“.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next we define a simple routine to get the information about the circuit "
"constructed for a quick check.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dále definujeme jednoduchou rutinu pro získání informací o sestaveném obvodu"
" pro rychlou kontrolu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let us exercise these routines.  You should see a circuit of 27 qubit "
"$\\times$ 15 layers (5 Trotter steps). Since the fake device has 28 edges, "
"there should be 28*5 entangling gages.\n"
msgstr ""
"Vyzkoušejme tyto rutiny. Měl bys vidět obvod o 27 qubitech $\\times$ 15 "
"vrstev (5 Trotterových kroků). Protože falešné zařízení má 28 hran, mělo by "
"být 28*5 provazujících hradel.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
